<FONT SIZE="2" FACE="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">
How's that for a self serving topic?  I have decided to write down some of my experineces on doing the shawl quest.  (Currently have the first shawl.)<P>Notes: Leat is a Druid (but you knew that)<P>To start the first quest you need to be indifferent to the dwarfs in Thor.  You can do this by killing Drakkel Dire Wolves but I've found that that is a big waste of time.<P>Start by killing Giants in the Great Divide next to the Eastern Waste zone.  Save the toes and the heads. . .just like everyone else.<BR>By the time you have 4 Gaint toes you will be indifferent or better to the dwarves and a lot closer to finishing your quest.<P>For the second shawl quest you need 10 giant heads.  You could have this mostly complete at the same time if you start hunting Giants.  (I ran into a fellow druid that had 10 heads and 2 sets of toes.)<P>Right now I have 8 heads.  At level 49 the green scouts give experience and I've made half a level just killing the stupid things.  They are very easy to kill, heck if it wasn't such a crowded zone I could quad kite them.  As it is I have over half my mana left when i solo one.<P>I spent the lower 40's in the EW hunting the Walrus's and when I got bored I ventured out and looked for other items for the third quest.  I have everything I need except for the 4 griffin eggs.
</FONT>
