File this under "Doh!"<P>Ok, today I finally get 4 griffin eggs and decide to give the quest another go.  Hell, by now I have enough snow bunny/tundra meat to do the quest about 6 more times.  They are sooooooo easy to come by.  (One snow bunny had less than 49 hit points.)<P>Let me back up a second and try to explain where I went wrong.<BR>Part 1 was to make a sandwich.  Easy.  No problems there.<BR>Part 2 was to make snow bunny stew.  By then I had several pots in my inventory.  They are all black and made with my smithing skill that I have just recently got up to 135.  Also in the bank I have a black pot that is Lore/No Drop from Mistmore.  They look the same.<P>When I was practicing my smithing skill, to make some pots, I moved everything I could into the bank so I would have more room in my inventory to play around with.  When I was done I moved a bunch of stuff back.<P>When you make the snow bunny stew you put a standard BLACK pot into the oven along with all your other stuff then hit combine and out pops a WHITE pot.  Lore/No drop.<P>I hand this to the NPC, get experience and a message then I checked my inventory.  No Dirty White pot in there.  Keep in mind that I had about 6 standard black pots, all of which were much lower down in my inventory.  (There were plenty of open spots in the bag that was in the first inventory slot.)<P>One of those black pots in my inventory was lore/no drop but it was black and I had assumed that it was the one from mistmore, since it was very far down in my inventory.  I figured I'd somehow got mixed up my inventory when I was moving all my stuff out of the bank.  So I tuck it back into the bank, and complain that the quest is broken.  (After I tried twice more to get the pot.)<P>I'm sure you know where this is going so I'll make it short.  Today I was moving stuff around in my bank and I noticed TWO lore/no drop BLACK pots.  *Doh*  one was the dirty pot I needed for the quest.<P>I tunred it in and (Imagine that!) it worked.<P>Ok, now for the bad news.  I had 4 griffin eggs and put them in the oven with the spices (unstacked of course)(baking skill at 135) and I FAILED!!!  I lacked the skill to make that item.<P>Oh well, back to hunting a rare spawn that only has a quarter chance of dropping an egg AND everyone else in the zone is also hunting.<P>You don't need to post. . .I feel stupid enough already.
