I finally finished the Third Shawl quest last night.  I spent most of the night gathering part for a pie tin so I could practice my baking skills.  Made 8 fruit pies without a single skill up and finally said F*** it. and tried the griffin soffle again.  It was NOT trivial at 135 baking skill but this time it was a success.<P>Turned in the soffle and got my items.  *Woot*  Now the only sucky item Leat has is on the Chest slot.<P>Some notes here.  I found hunting for Griffins just east of the Orc fort was the best location.  The first time I tried this I would run the length of the zone just East of the bridge and it took about 12 hours to find the griffins.  While hunting around the Orc fort it took about 4 hours.  It did help that the drop rate was about 1 in every two or three griffins the second time compared to 1 in 4 the first.<P>More advice.  When you are hunting Kodiaks (sp?) for the Sandwich, save any HQ pelts you might pick up along the way.  There is quite a market out there for them because of the Ring Quest.  Also there are a lot of stupid people out there that don't know the Snow Bunnies are level 2 or 3 and will pay big bucks for their meat. heheh  (Even after I tell them that they still want to buy them because they are too lazy.)<BR>Killing stuff in the zone DOES help the spawn rate of the griffins.  (one reason they spawn near the Orc fort) so while you are tracking them be sure to kill and the little snow bunnies along the way.<P>I'm not going to attempt the fourth shawl for a while.  I think I'm I'm going to work on my tayloring skill and perhaps play around a little in CC when I get bored.<P>One last note on this.  I have another Seal that you get when you start this quest.  I'd like to use it to see if you can multi-quest this stuff.  Here is the deal.  I hand in the seal and get the napkin.  Then I give someone the stuff to make the sandwich (Hell I have enough of it in the bank!)  They make the sandwich, we head to the NPC.  They give them the sandwich, I give them the napkin and we see what happens.<P>Let me know if you are interested in trying this.
