The 3rd shawl is multiquestable in several ways. The seal that you get at the beginning of the quest you can get as many times as you want remember. Just ask for it and he'll give it to you. The best way to do this is to have someone that has high baking skills to make the various foods. And the non skilled person turn in the napkins. This is waht Cura and I did. I made the food, turned in the food and then he would turn in the napkin.<P>Or for someone that already has the 3rd shawl and the Seal of Thordain(This is the better item 3wis 3int 30mana/range slot). If they don't want their seal anymore you can just have them turn in their seal, then the other person turn in their shawl and you have skipped the entire food making parts for the second person.<P>They way you described multiquesting it wouldn't work, since some of the food items that get made are no drop. One thing Cura and I found out the hard way is that you must be indifferent to start the first quest. Which seemed really stupid to me, turning in the heads and toes should be a way to get faction, well it is but you need to already have decent faction to get anymore faction.<P>--------------------<P><B>Nefarius Draconocissor</B> - 54 Wanderer/Freelance Gynocologist <BR><B>Meretrixx</B> - 48 Warrior<BR>Bertoxxolus
